2026-08-28 novel-peptide validation
Inputs: 4 supplied MGF files (169,591 spectra total), 196 supplied candidate peptides, supplied human UniProt+isoforms FASTA (147,506 entries), supplied cRAP FASTA (116 entries), SGPS and MaxQuant peptide reports.
Input integrity: human and cRAP SHA-256 values match the supplied manifest.
Engine: PepQuery2 2.0.2 (Bioconda package hdfd78af_0).
Search: novel-peptide mode; title index; trypsin; 2 missed cleavages; precursor 10 ppm; fragment 0.6 Da; CID/HCD; charge 2-6; fixed PTMs 1,13,14 (Carbamidomethyl C, TMT 11-plex K, TMT 11-plex peptide N-term); variable PTM 2 (Oxidation M); HyperScore; stringent UMS competition; amino-acid-substitution competition; remaining PepQuery defaults.
Reference: decompressed supplied human FASTA concatenated with supplied cRAP FASTA (147,622 entries).
Verification rule: peptide has at least one PepQuery psm_rank row with confident=Yes across the four supplied fractions.
Assignment rule: collect SGPS columns Sequence/Protein(s) and MaxQuant columns Sequence/Proteins; split multi-protein fields; normalize UniProt pipe records to accessions; deduplicate peptide-accession pairs.
Resource strategy: F10 completed against the monolithic reference. Later monolithic attempts were killed under host memory pressure. The supplied reference was therefore digested with PepQuery's bundled CompOmics iterator and searched as exact spectrum-specific subsets: 10-ppm subsets for standard competition and 500-Da precursor bins expanded by 252 Da on each side for PepQuery's unrestricted-modification window. Target peptide-spectrum pairs were title-restricted within each bin. This preserves all possible competitors while reducing peak memory; all 82 F10 PSM confidence calls from this strategy exactly matched the monolithic F10 calls.
Results: 134 unique peptides had at least one confident PSM across F10/F11/F13/F15. Report mapping produced 139 unique microbial peptide-accession pairs; every verified peptide had at least one supplied microbial assignment.
Deliverable QC: exactly 2 tab-separated columns; 139 data rows; uppercase unannotated peptide sequences; no empty IDs; no duplicate pairs. SHA-256 verified_peptides.tsv = 9553035b93658370d9024b0c6b4d09e43c470716d2677154dcfc8949b53280c7.
